messages.reasoning_content:
Interesting U+00FF returns -1? unicodeRanges second {begin 0x80,end 0xFF} excludes 0xFF end exclusive, and first ends 0x7F, so 0xFF unassigned. Weird but not relevant. U+4E00 index59 -> range2 bit27=0x08000000. U+10000 index101 -> range4 bit5=0x20. U+1D400 index89 -> range3 bit25=0x02000000. U+E000 index60 -> range2 bit28=0x10000000. Could test multiple glyphs with different ranges: A range0, U+E000 range2, U+1D400 range3, U+10000 range4. Then expect:
ulUnicodeRange1 = 1
ulUnicodeRange2 = 1 << (60-32)=1<<28=0x10000000
